<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">18 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 18 August, from 684 to 1963.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">684 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,342 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Umayyads defeat the supporters of Ibn al-Zubayr at Marj Rahit</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-fitna">Second Fitna</a>, the Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> Marwan I and his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-kalb">Kalb</a> allies defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qays">Qays</a> tribes, who backed the Mecca-based caliph <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-allah-ibn-al-zubayr">Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr</a>, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>. The victory secured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyads</a> but fuelled a long Qays–Kalb feud.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-marj-rahit-684">Battle of Marj Rahit</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-fitna">Second Fitna</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-allah-ibn-al-zubayr">Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1227">1227 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">799 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Genghis Khan dies during his campaign against the Tangut</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> died during the siege of the Western Xia, traditionally on this date. He had built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>, which under his heirs became the largest contiguous land empire in history.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1304">1304 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">722 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Philip IV of France fights the Flemish at Mons-en-Pévèle</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">South of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lille">Lille</a>, the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-iv-of-france">Philip IV of France</a> fought the Flemish militias that had defeated the French at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kortrijk">Kortrijk</a> two years earlier. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-athis-sur-orge">Treaty of Athis-sur-Orge</a> of 1305 afterwards imposed heavy penalties on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mons-en-pevele">Battle of Mons-en-Pévèle</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1492">1492 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">534 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nebrija dates the preface of the first Spanish grammar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-de-nebrija">Elio Antonio de Nebrija</a> dated the introduction to his Gramática de la lengua castellana, written in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salamanca">Salamanca</a> and the first grammar of a modern European language, writing that language was always the companion of empire. He presented it to Queen Isabella I.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-language">Spanish language</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isabella-i-of-castile">Isabella I of Castile</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1572">1572 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">454 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry of Navarre marries Margaret of Valois in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Protestant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-france">Henry of Navarre</a> married the Catholic princess Margaret, sister of Charles IX, a union meant to reconcile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>'s factions. Six days later the St Bartholomew's Day massacre began.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1868">1868 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">158 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Solar eclipse observations reveal the element later named helium</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Observing a total solar eclipse in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, Jules Janssen saw an unexplained yellow line in the Sun's spectrum. Norman Lockyer attributed it to a new element, helium, not found on Earth until 1895.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1920">1920 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">106 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tennessee ratifies the 19th Amendment, giving US women the vote</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a> became the 36th state to ratify, by one vote cast by a young legislator heeding his mother's letter. The amendment barred denial of the vote on account of sex.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1963">1963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">James Meredith graduates from the University of Mississippi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">James Meredith became the first Black graduate of Ole Miss. His enrolment in 1962 had provoked a deadly riot and required thousands of federal troops to enforce.</p></div></li></ol>
